                <pb facs="0203" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1907p1/pg91"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 836/46.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Chargé Lorillard</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1907-01-10"><hi rendition="#italic">January 10,
                        1907</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Bacon states that the action of the President of Brazil decreeing the
                    continuance of the preferential tariff is highly appreciated as evidence of
                    friendly good will.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
